# The "eitri" account runs the unauthenticated configurator, Moonraker, Klipper, Klarity and the camera
# programs, so a flaw in any of them must not hand out root. It gets exactly these:
#
#   - the two on-device update tools, without a password (they do the boot-slot and RAUC work;
#     unit control, reboot, host name and networking go through polkit, see
#     usr/share/polkit-1/rules.d/50-eitri.rules). Through sudo, eitri-update refuses every option that
#     changes what is trusted or where root writes (--config, --manifest-url, --key-dir, --data-root,
#     --allow-insecure, --allow-downgrade, another --events-file), and it never runs anything from
#     /data as root: overlay-install.sh, spi_flash.py, firmware builds and git in the service user's
#     trees run as the service user (eitri_mcuflash/privs.py);
#   - optional shell access (decision 4): the configurator adds an SSH key or sets a password through
#     eitri-access, one fixed command line per rule (sudo matches the arguments exactly, so there is no
#     way to add others). The key or password is read from stdin and validated by the tool;
#   - "unlock setup" (decision 8): Klarity's button runs `eitri-configurator unlock`. It runs the
#     configurator's own copy in the read-only image, never code from /data, drops to the eitri user
#     before it touches the maintenance flag under /data/eitri/configurator, and starts the service;
#   - an administrator key for the separate "admin" account (sudoers.d/admin), but only during
#     first setup: admin-set-key refuses once the window is closed, and closing it is one-way.
#
# Nothing else. "eitri" has NO general sudo rule, not even behind a password: it can set its own
# password (eitri-access set-password), so a password-protected "ALL" rule would let any program it
# runs make itself root. Root is the "admin" account's job. Do not add an ALL rule for "eitri";
# os/tests/test_tree.py rejects it. Bench images that need one ship it in a separate drop-in
# (sudoers.d/eitri-dev).
eitri ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/eitri-update, /usr/libexec/eitri/eitri-bootctl
eitri ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/libexec/eitri/eitri-access set-key, /usr/libexec/eitri/eitri-access disable, /usr/libexec/eitri/eitri-access status
eitri ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/libexec/eitri/eitri-access admin-set-key, /usr/libexec/eitri/eitri-access admin-close-window
eitri ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/libexec/eitri/eitri-access set-password, /usr/libexec/eitri/eitri-access set-password --ssh-login
eitri ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/eitri-configurator unlock
